Subject: [PATCH] input: native DualSense / DualShock 4 (HID), with the game's vibration

Ported from our earlier recomp (patches 0015, 0234, 0242: ps2_sony_pad.h, ps2_sony_pad.cpp,
ps2_sony_pad_host.cpp; GPL-3.0 like PS2Recomp). DualSense, DualSense Edge and DualShock 4 over
USB or Bluetooth are read over Windows HID on a thread of their own (no Steam Input or
DS4Windows): every button, both sticks, the analog triggers; the light bar takes a colour; the
game's libpad actuators (scePadSetActAlign / scePadSetActDirect, no-ops before) drive the
motors. Without a Sony pad the GLFW gamepads read as before.

Adapted to this runtime: the pad read keeps its own button map (the Sony pad fills the same
list as a GLFW gamepad, keyboard and mouse on top); settings are environment variables
(PS2X_GAMEPAD_BACKEND auto|glfw|sony, PS2X_SONYPAD_RUMBLE 0..100, PS2X_SONYPAD_LIGHTBAR
RRGGBB|off, PS2X_SONYPAD_TRACE=1), not our earlier recomp's [gamepad] section.

